# Existing behavior preservation

The admin app is working. Success is the requested change plus everything else unchanged.

Do not change, unless the task asks: routing, fixtures, page copy, loading and empty states, layout, or shared component behavior. Do not rename nearby symbols, restyle a page, or rewrite a working component to “clean it up.”

```text
❌ BAD — the task adds a button, and the edit also renames helpers and restyles the page
✅ GOOD — add the button and the wiring it needs
```

- Inspect the component and its call sites before editing. Extend it; do not replace it.
- If two readings would change behavior that was not requested, ask.
- Report unrelated bugs; do not fix them in the same change.
- After a code change, run `npm run typecheck`, `npm run lint`, and `npm run format:check` in `admin/` when the edit can affect them. Fix regressions you caused.
